RC receiver module reads the PWM signals from a receiver connected to the STM32 and receiver has 4 channels: steering, throttle, teleoperation and a deadman switch. The STM32 measures signal pulse width using interrupts and a timer. The measurements it gets are put inside arrays, then into the packet for transmission. 
File areas:
  firmware/include/recieverinput.h — data structure and function declarations
  firmware/src/recieverinput.cpp — receiver initialization, PWM measurement, and packet updates
  
  Hardware and pins

Receiver    pin(stm32)    intention
CH1			pa0		steering
CH2			PA1		throttle
CH3			PA3		teloperation status
CH4			PA4		deadman switch (scary name)...


